From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tristin Baker <tristinbaker@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:12:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add OE_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_MOUSE: use a gamepad's touchpad as
 the mouse

For platforms without a mouse (the PS5). The SDL2 backend turns touchpad input into mouse events, like a laptop
touchpad: a finger moves the pointer by its travel, pressing the pad left-clicks, pressing it with two fingers on
it right-clicks, and repeated presses double-click. The pointer stays put while the pad is pressed, so clicks
don't drag it off their target. SdlWindow::warpMouse and real mouse motion move the touchpad pointer as well.

The game then always draws the arrow cursor itself and hides it after 3 seconds without mouse movement, and keeps
the pointer inside the letterboxed picture. The custom arrow is now drawn with its tip, not its centre, at the
pointer, which also fixes always_custom_cursor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
